SUMMARY:NJYS Jazz Concert
DESCRIPTION:NJYS Jazz Concert\nDecember 6\, 2026 at 3:00 p.m.\nSieminski Theater\, Basking Ridge\n$20/Adults\, $15/Students & Seniors\nClick HERE for tickets (Coming Soon) \nExperience the energy\, artistry\, and joy of jazz with the New Jersey Youth Symphony Jazz Program! Featuring our talented Jazz Orchestra\, Big Band\, and Jazz Workshop students\, this concert brings to life works by Art Blakey\, Duke Ellington\, Miles Davis\, Thelonious Monk\, Charlie Parker\, Jackie McLean\, Juan Tizol and more. Come support these remarkable young musicians and enjoy the vibrant sounds of jazz as they continue their musical journey toward greatness!\nJazz Orchestra: Shamie Royston\, Director\nBig Band: Gregory Williams\, Director\nJazz Workshop: Dave Schumacher\, Director \n 
URL:https://whartonarts.org/calendar/njys-jazz-concert-2/
LOCATION:Sieminski Theater at Fellowship Village\, 8000 Fellowship Rd\, Basking Ridge\, NJ\, 07920\, United States
