SUMMARY:NJYS Music Across Generations
DESCRIPTION:NJYS Music Across Generations\nFebruary 21\, 2027 at 5:00 pm\nNicholas Music Center\, Rutgers University\n$20/Adults\, $15/Students & Seniors\nClick HERE for tickets (Coming Soon) \nMusic connects us across time\, across generations\, and across the many chapters of our lives. In this joyful celebration of our Season of Hope\, mother-son piano duo\, Two Piano Journey: Michelle Chen Kuo & Christopher Kuo\, joins the NJYS Youth Symphony for Poulenc’s brilliant and playful Concerto for Two Pianos. \nThe concert also brings the extended NJYS family together on one stage with the NJYS Community Orchestra\, featuring parents\, alumni\, staff\, and students making music side by side. It’s a celebration of what we receive\, what we share\, and what we pass on to the next generation. \n 
URL:https://whartonarts.org/calendar/njys-music-across-generations/
LOCATION:Nicholas Music Center at Rutgers New Brunswick\, 85 George St\, New Brunswick\, NJ\, 08901\, United States
CATEGORIES:NJYS,NJYS Alumni,Wharton
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://whartonarts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/2_21--scaled.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="NJYS":MAILTO:info@NJYS.org
END:VEVENT
